+    }
+    if (videoCh->states.waitingKeyFrame == 0) {
+        /* A backward sequence is an old frame the host re-sent (a duplicate): drop it
+         * silently without touching our tracking. A FORWARD jump means frames were lost.
+         * The original code hard-waited for a keyframe on ANY forward gap and then dropped
+         * EVERY frame until a full IDR arrived (the guard below) — a multi-frame freeze for
+         * a 1-frame blip, firing ~once a second on a good link: the "borderline unplayable"
+         * brief stutter. Instead ask for a keyframe once (to heal cleanly) but KEEP DECODING
